# review-toolkit config: copy to review.env (gitignored) and fill in. Sourced by review-env.sh.
# Any of these already set in the environment wins over this file.
#
# Every allowlist is empty by default, and an empty allowlist refuses every post. Fill them
# in only for the people and repos who agreed to the auto-post experiment.

# --- who and where ------------------------------------------------------------------------
AUTO_POST_AUTHORS=""          # comma list of PR author logins review-post.sh may review
AUTO_POST_REPOS=""            # comma list of owner/repo both wrappers may post in
# AUTO_POST_SELF=""           # your GitHub login; empty means ask `gh api user`
AUTO_POST_TEAMS=""            # comma list of your own team slugs; a request to one counts as yours

# --- inline comment labels ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every inline comment must open with one of these (after any leading `> ...` header lines).
# Default: the original four plus the Conventional Comments labels.
# AUTO_POST_LABELS="must-fix,should-fix,nit,question,issue,suggestion,nitpick,thought,todo,praise,chore,note"

# --- reply guardrails ---------------------------------------------------------------------
AUTO_POST_HEADER="Automated review"   # every reply body must contain this text
AUTO_POST_MAX_REPLIES=2               # header-carrying replies per thread before escalating

# --- off switch ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# While this file exists both wrappers refuse (exit 10) before any GitHub call.
# AUTO_POST_KILL_SWITCH="$HOME/.claude/mission-control/auto-post.off"

# Optional: where the work log helper lives. Default: ../mission-control/worklog.sh.
# AUTO_POST_WORKLOG=""
